  "result": "Based on my investigation of the codebase, I found where the refusals are handled and where the expiry setting is configured.\n\nWhen a user clicks an invitation link, the acceptance flow goes through:\n1. The invite page (`src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`) displays the form\n2. The form calls the `acceptInvitationAction` \n3. This action invokes `acceptInvitation` from the **invitation service**\n\nIn `src/server/services/invitation-service.ts`, the `acceptInvitation` function validates the invitation token and throws three specific error messages (lines 127-135):\n- \"That invitation has been revoked\" (for cancelled invitations)\n- \"That invitation has already been accepted\" (for already-used links)  \n- \"That invitation has expired\" (for old links)\n\nThe same file also defines the expiry setting:\n- Line 26: `DEFAULT_EXPIRY_DAYS = 14` - This is the setting that determines how old is \"too old\"\n\nThis constant is used when creating invitations (line 93) to set their expiry time, and the `acceptInvitation` function compares the current time against `invitation.expiresAt` to reject expired invitations.\n\nANSWER: src/server/services/invitation-service.ts",
